    "winner": "01__19559969-SUPPLEMENTAL-RESP.PRE-V1-10142026.tex",
    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Since all candidate documents are functionally identical (Candidates 2 through 5 simply input Candidate 1), Candidate 1 is selected by default. The document correctly addresses several formal requirements, including the submission of a substitute specification with a no-new-matter certification under 37 CFR 1.125, reaffirmation of Small Entity status under 37 CFR 1.27, and the filing of a 5-month extension of time petition under 37 CFR 1.136(a). However, the document contains a fatal strategic flaw regarding the payment of statutory filing fees.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": "The candidate is highly unlikely to succeed because it explicitly refuses to pay the outstanding basic filing fees, instead requesting that the Office defer the balance to a new 37 CFR 1.53(f) Notice of Fee Deficiency. The application is already under a Notice to File Missing Parts (mailed 2026-04-03) and a Notice of Incomplete Reply (mailed 2026-08-12). The statutory period for reply, including the maximum 5-month extension, expires on 2026-11-03. The USPTO will not issue a second Notice to File Missing Parts to reset the clock; failure to remit the full required filing fees by the deadline will result in irrevocable abandonment.",
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "The candidate aligns with the ATS brief by filing the substitute specification, asserting Small Entity status, and petitioning for the 5-month extension of time. However, it directly violates the critical ATS directive to remit the net Small Entity filing fee balance of $590.00, opting instead for an invalid legal strategy of deferring the fees.",
    "candidate_scores": [
      {
        "candidate": "01__19559969-SUPPLEMENTAL-RESP.PRE-V1-10142026.tex",
